    "site_desc": "The Cedar Bridge flux tower is located in an upland, pitch pine stand in the New Jersey pine barrens. The stand was burned in wildfires in 1963 and 1995, and experienced eastern pine looper defoliation in 1998. Disturbance history since the tower's establishment includes (1) prescribed fires in 2008, 2013, 2020, and 2024, (2) spongy moth (Lymantria dispar) defoliation of understory  oaks in 2007, and (3) wind, snow storms, and drought.",
